+---
+title: Adding a built-in ParamType (click.Duration)
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 49951 }
+touches:
+  - CHANGES.md
+  - docs/api.md
+  - docs/parameter-types.md
+  - src/click/__init__.py
+  - src/click/types.py
+  - tests/test_types.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- New built-in types live in src/click/types.py next to their closest sibling (Duration sits after DateTime), get a `__repr__`, use `_()` for fail messages, and are re-exported in src/click/__init__.py with the `from .types import X as X` form.
+- Docs go in two places: the "Built-in Types Listing" in docs/parameter-types.md (`*   .. autoclass:: X` + `:noindex:`) and the types section of docs/api.md.
+- CHANGES.md had no unreleased section after 8.5.0; a "Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased" section was opened and the docstring uses `.. versionadded:: 8.6`. Confirm the version number with the maintainer.
+- Duration accepts only str or timedelta; ints (e.g. `default=60`) fail, per the spec given.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- `\d` / `$` in the duration regex: `\d` matches non-ASCII digits and `$` matches before a trailing newline. Use `[0-9]` with `re.fullmatch`, and `str.isascii() and isdigit()` for the bare-seconds form.
+
+## Watch out
+- An all-optional-groups regex fullmatches the empty string; require at least one group to be non-None.
+- `timedelta(days=huge)` raises OverflowError; catch it and route to `self.fail` so the user gets a BadParameter.
+- The test run reports ~31000 deselected tests. Those are stress tests excluded by `addopts = "-m 'not stress'"`, not a broken selection.
